# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repo *and* in the working tree.
#
# This is not a style preference. The tool runs on a Linux printer host, and
# src/updatefw.py has a `#!/usr/bin/env python3` shebang: if that file ever
# reaches the Pi with CRLF endings, the kernel reads the interpreter as
# "python3\r" and you get
#
#     bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env python3^M: No such file or directory
#
# Pinning eol=lf here means every clone behaves the same regardless of that
# machine's core.autocrlf, and stops Git warning about the conversion on
# Windows checkouts (this project is developed on Windows).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary, so Git never tries to translate them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.bin binary
*.uf2 binary
*.pyc binary
